# The in-picker bindings, which are compiled in and not read from a config.
# The Ctrl-r / Ctrl-t shell integration only exists once you source fzf's
# key-bindings file — until then the first group here does nothing.
name:    fzf
what:    fuzzy picker. Pipe it a list, get back the one you chose
check:   fzf
install: sudo dnf install fzf   /   sudo apt install fzf
docs:    man fzf

= THE SHELL BINDINGS — the reason to install it
Ctrl-r           | fuzzy-search your shell history. Replaces the plain Ctrl-r
Ctrl-t           | pick a file and paste its path into the line you are typing
Alt-c            | pick a directory and cd there
cmd **<Tab>      | complete that command's argument through fzf

= INSIDE THE PICKER
type             | narrow the list as you go; letters need not be adjacent
Up / Down        | move the selection
Enter            | choose it
Esc or Ctrl-c    | cancel, choosing nothing
Tab              | mark this one and move on, when multi-select is enabled
Shift-Tab        | unmark
Ctrl-a           | select everything shown
Ctrl-/           | move the preview pane, or hide it
Shift-Up/Down    | scroll the preview

= SEARCH SYNTAX
abc              | fuzzy: those letters in that order, gaps allowed
'abc             | exact substring
^abc             | starts with
abc$             | ends with
!abc             | does NOT contain
a \| b           | a or b
